 effort and  the gsb is definitely one of those  places where collaboration is  part of the experience right how do you  support others  and challenge each other to grow to the  fullest extent  i mean the policy of grade  non-disclosure really exemplifies that  you know not publishing lists of gpa or  class rank to recruiters  this frees you to help each other to ask  for help  and to create that support network so  you're always lifting each other up  and you're part of it and you should be  the center of this discussion  so don't worry about not feeling like  you're being a teammate by using the  phrase i  i really do want to know about what you  did and how you did it  so networking interview two  parts of the application process that  are going to be  um really dependent and really fueled by  your voice  um so definitely practice find someone  you trust  maybe this is an instance where you  practice on that networking side  invite someone at work to a one-on-one  so you can learn more about  their kind of job responsibilities and  role  sometimes you know loki interviewing  like that  will help you as someone who's speaking  on the other end you know  feel comfortable about you know this is  just a conversation  talking to people really does help with  this and i know that might be exhausting  for some  it might be energizing for others so  find those times  where you know you're willing to exert  that and find those times where you  and honor the times you just need to  recharge  and this brings us here  so when i started uh you know  in admissions like i there was a lot of  learning  i realized that as i was growing up i  knew actually nothing about what it  meant to apply to college  or even grad school it often felt like  looking back there might have been some  kind of hidden curriculum to  how to get in and how to thrive  and so my goal with the events this week  and my goal  with um the sharing your story series  was to illuminate the process  so that you